{title: 222 - Hark! Ten Thousand Harps and Voices}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Hark! ten thousand harps and [C]voices
Sound the [F]note of [C7]praise a[F]bove;
[F]Jesus reigns, and heaven re[C]joices,
Jesus [F]reigns, the [C7]God of [F]love:
[C]See, He [C7]sits on yonder throne;
[F]Jesus rules the world alone.
Alleluia! Alle[C]luia!
Alle[F]luia! [C7]A[F]men.

Verse 2:
[F]King of [C]glory, reign forever,
[F]Thine [C7]an [F]everlasting crown;
[F]Nothing from Thy [C]love shall sever
[F]Those whom [C7]Thou hast [F]made Thine own;
[C]Happy objects [C7]of Thy grace,
[F]Destined to behold Thy face.
[C]Alleluia! Alleluia!
[F][C7]Alleluia! [F]Amen.

Verse 3:
[F]Savior, hasten [C]Thine appearing;
[F]Bring, O [C7]bring the [F]glorious day,
[F]When, the [C]awful summons hearing,
[F]Heaven and [C7]earth shall [F]pass away:;
[C]Then, with golden [C7]harps we'll sing,
[F]"Glory, glory to our King!"
[C]Alleluia! Alleluia!
[F][C7]Alleluia! [F]Amen.
